    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "fd4e7f11729ae2da62a417d68940d8f8a263c476",
            "parents": [
                "4d2da4bef6656b6b71ecfc09ef8a416ccece50b9"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/38/85038/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "createdOn": 1762511902,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm considering adding a short delay (e.g., sleep 60) before executing the reboot, to provide a window for users to capture diagnostics in case the system repeatedly enters the BMC Quiesced state and would otherwise fall into a reboot loop."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why wouldn't we run the reboot target (or an openbmc-specific target that calls reboot) and if people want to add diagnostics inside there, they can do that?  Or, I guess people can add Before/Wants to this service if they want to run things?  \n\nI'm not sure why we'd want to add an arbitrary delay.  These things can be solved with systemd dependencies."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Understood. Platforms can add a drop-in (e.g., ExecStartPre or a service with Before=reboot.target and Wants/Requires) to run pre-reboot diagnostics. Thanks for the suggestion."
                },
                {
                    "file": "service_files/phosphor-bmc-quiesce-reboot.service",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Where is the code to trigger this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "service_files/phosphor-bmc-quiesce-reboot.service",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I added a Meson option \u201cauto-reboot-on-bmc-quiesce\u201d (disabled by default) that installs a wants symlink so entering Quiesced pulls in the reboot service (scoped to @0)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "service_files/phosphor-bmc-quiesce-reboot.service",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Should this be /sbin/reboot or should it be a dependency on the reboot.target or start the reboot.target?  Should we run `systemctl reboot` instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "service_files/phosphor-bmc-quiesce-reboot.service",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "`/sbin/reboot` is a symlink to `systemctl reboot` anyhow on systemd installs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "service_files/phosphor-bmc-quiesce-reboot.service",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I switched the unit to use:\n```\nExecStart=/usr/bin/systemctl reboot\n```\nas it\u2019s more explicit than /sbin/reboot. If preferred, I can change it to start reboot.target instead."
                }
            ],
